{"kind":"doc","route":"/resources/roadmap","title":"Roadmap","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"roadmap","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Roadmap"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"@craft-ts/core is evolving through real-world usage, careful experimentation,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"and feedback from the community. This roadmap describes the areas I am"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"currently planning to explore; it is intentionally not a promise of fixed"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"release dates."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"near-term-priorities","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Near-term priorities"}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"ssr-as-a-craft-host","children":[{"t":"text","text":"SSR as a Craft host"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"SSR is a Craft deployment concern: serialize Craft trees to HTML at the runtime"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"boundary."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"That work lives in a later compiler/host plan; this release does not ship a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"product SSR renderer."}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"real-world-integration-and-stability","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Real-world integration and stability"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"I will continue integrating "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/core"},{"t":"text","text":" into projects so that I can"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"experiment with the different situations and constraints that applications"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"encounter in practice. This ongoing use should help uncover edge cases,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"validate the API, and move the library towards the most stable version"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"possible."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"I am also studying improvements that could make the codebase more robust. I"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"am open to suggestions, proposals, and discussions about changes that would"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"improve reliability, maintainability, or the developer experience."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"type-safe-design-systems","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Type-safe design systems"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Another area I am actively exploring is how to create a design system that is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"as type-safe as possible. The aim is to make design-system APIs expressive and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"safe to use while preserving a good development experience."}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Improve the type-level techniques used by the library so that they are more"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"efficient. In particular, I want to reduce type compilation time and make"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the feedback loop faster for developers."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"One current challenge is TypeScript's memory limitation. A very ambitious"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"type-level design can place a significant load on the TypeScript compiler, so"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"this constraint has to be considered alongside the benefits of stronger"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"inference."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"If you have ideas for addressing this problem, I would be very happy to hear"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"them. Please feel free to share your opinions and suggestions. I am willing"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"to introduce utilities or adaptations where necessary to make promising"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"approaches compatible with the library and practical to use."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"tooling-for-understanding-changes","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Tooling for understanding changes"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"I also plan to create a precise dependency graph and a tool that can compare"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"two branches. The goal is to make the changes introduced by artificial"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"intelligence easier to inspect and understand, by providing a clearer view of"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the affected dependencies and the differences between two versions of a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"codebase."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"I may also extend the dependency graph to represent complete paths through the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"graph, making it possible to follow how a change propagates across the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"codebase. This could provide a foundation for adding architecture tests and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"architecture constraints directly to the same tooling, so that intended"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"dependencies and boundaries can be checked automatically."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"I am also considering building DevTools for "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/core"},{"t":"text","text":", although I am"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"not yet certain how valuable a traditional DevTools experience would be for"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the library. If there are features or workflows you would find useful in this"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"area, please feel free to tell me about them."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Several of my current ideas are more AI-first: tools designed to help an AI"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"agent debug an application through WebMCP and observability, for example by"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"making runtime state, dependency relationships, and application events easier"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"to inspect and reason about. Feedback will help determine whether these ideas"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"should become part of a DevTools experience or evolve as separate tools."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"typed-streams-craft-ts-stream","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Typed streams ("},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/stream"},{"t":"text","text":")"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A typed RxJS-like library built around the principles of "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/core"},{"t":"text","text":" now"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"exists: "},{"t":"code","text":"CraftStream<A, Y>"},{"t":"text","text":" is a cold push stream whose type accumulates the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"service dependencies of its operators' handlers and the typed exceptions they"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"may raise — readable at the terminal, where "},{"t":"code","text":"subscribe"},{"t":"text","text":" refuses to compile"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"without a handler for every exception. See "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/reactivity/streams","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Typed streams"}]},{"t":"text","text":"."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Delivered: the carrier and "},{"t":"code","text":".pipe"},{"t":"text","text":" (up to 14 operators); per-value operators ("},{"t":"code","text":"map"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"filter"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"tap"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"scan"},{"t":"text","text":"); selection ("},{"t":"code","text":"take"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"skip"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"takeWhile"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"distinctUntilChanged"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"startWith"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"pairwise"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"takeUntil"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"takeUntilDestroyed"},{"t":"text","text":"); flattening ("},{"t":"code","text":"switchMap"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"exhaustMap"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"concatMap"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"mergeMap"},{"t":"text","text":"); combination ("},{"t":"code","text":"combineLatest"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"merge"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"zip"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"race"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"withLatestFrom"},{"t":"text","text":"); time ("},{"t":"code","text":"debounce"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"throttle"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"delay"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"timeout"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"retry"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"repeat"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"auditTime"},{"t":"text","text":"); sources ("},{"t":"code","text":"interval"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"timer"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"fromEvent"},{"t":"text","text":"); grouping ("},{"t":"code","text":"buffer"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"bufferCount"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"bufferTime"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"bufferWhen"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"sample"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"groupBy"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"window"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"windowCount"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"expand"},{"t":"text","text":"); exceptions ("},{"t":"code","text":"catchTag"},{"t":"text","text":" and "},{"t":"code","text":".exhaustive"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"mapException"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"orElse"},{"t":"text","text":");"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"multicast ("},{"t":"code","text":"share"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"shareReplay"},{"t":"text","text":"); the terminals ("},{"t":"code","text":"lastValueFrom"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"firstValueFrom"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"toArray"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"runForEach"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"subscribe"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"streamSignal"},{"t":"text","text":"); the Effect adapters"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"("},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/stream-effect"},{"t":"text","text":"); and the "},{"t":"code","text":"craft-migrate-streams"},{"t":"text","text":" codemod. Core no longer"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"depends on RxJS."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Also delivered: the everyday operators ("},{"t":"code","text":"first"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"last"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"takeLast"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"reduce"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"skipWhile"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"skipUntil"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"distinct"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"defaultIfEmpty"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"ignoreElements"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"endWith"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"finalize"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"switchAll"},{"t":"text","text":"/"},{"t":"code","text":"mergeAll"},{"t":"text","text":"/"},{"t":"code","text":"concatAll"},{"t":"text","text":"/"},{"t":"code","text":"exhaustAll"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"concat"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"concatWith"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"mergeWith"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"combineLatestWith"},{"t":"text","text":") and the creators "},{"t":"code","text":"defer"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"throwError"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"never"},{"t":"text","text":". The codemod now also"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"moves "},{"t":"code","text":"lastValueFrom"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"throwError"},{"t":"text","text":" and "},{"t":"code","text":"asyncScheduler"},{"t":"text","text":"-taking calls over."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Also delivered: "},{"t":"code","text":"materialize"},{"t":"text","text":" / "},{"t":"code","text":"dematerialize"},{"t":"text","text":" (with a "},{"t":"code","text":"'X'"},{"t":"text","text":" notification for typed"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"exceptions), "},{"t":"code","text":"observeOn"},{"t":"text","text":" / "},{"t":"code","text":"subscribeOn"},{"t":"text","text":" (they hop onto the temporal runtime — craft's one"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"scheduler, so there is no scheduler argument), and the connectable family ("},{"t":"code","text":"connectable"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"publish"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"publishReplay"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"publishBehavior"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"multicast"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"refCount"},{"t":"text","text":"). The codemod"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"translates all of them, dropping rxjs scheduler arguments with a review notice."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Also delivered: the creators "},{"t":"code","text":"from"},{"t":"text","text":" (a stream, a Subscribable, a Promise or an iterable),"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"fromPromise"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"fromIterable"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"generate"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"bindCallback"},{"t":"text","text":" / "},{"t":"code","text":"bindNodeCallback"},{"t":"text","text":" and "},{"t":"code","text":"fromFetch"},{"t":"text","text":";"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the codemod translates "},{"t":"code","text":"from"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"scheduled"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"generate"},{"t":"text","text":" (positional form included),"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"bindCallback"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"fromFetch"},{"t":"text","text":", and a publish-family operator wherever it sits in a pipe."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Also delivered: "},{"t":"code","text":"ajax"},{"t":"text","text":" ("},{"t":"code","text":"getJSON"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"get"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"post"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"put"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"patch"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"delete"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"AjaxError"},{"t":"text","text":") and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"webSocket"},{"t":"text","text":" — stream-shaped network sources on "},{"t":"code","text":"fetch"},{"t":"text","text":" and the platform "},{"t":"code","text":"WebSocket"},{"t":"text","text":" — and the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"connect(selector, { connector })"},{"t":"text","text":" operator, which is where the selector forms of "},{"t":"code","text":"publish"},{"t":"text","text":","},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"publishReplay"},{"t":"text","text":" and "},{"t":"code","text":"multicast"},{"t":"text","text":" land. The codemod now also expands aliased and namespace"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"imports (renaming every reference), and wraps a "},{"t":"code","text":".pipe"},{"t":"text","text":" receiver whose type it cannot"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"establish in "},{"t":"code","text":"from(...)"},{"t":"text","text":" with a review notice instead of refusing the file."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The codemod's one remaining boundary is the one every all-or-nothing migration has: a symbol"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"that is in none of its tables (a future rxjs export, a third-party operator) leaves the file"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"untouched, with a diagnostic naming the symbol — and an alias that clashes with another name"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"in the file, a namespace used as a plain value, or an operator taking a form that cannot be"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"expressed (a "},{"t":"code","text":"publishReplay"},{"t":"text","text":" with three arguments before its selector) do the same."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"longer-term-exploration-type-safe-server-functions","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Longer-term exploration: type-safe server functions"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Further ahead, I am considering a server-function system built around the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"same principles. The idea is to allow dependency injection in server"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"functions while keeping it fully type-safe."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Such a system could also allow the server function to depend on data supplied"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"by the front end. That data would be passed automatically and checked in a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"type-safe way, so the contract between the client and the server remains"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"explicit and reliable from end to end."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"This is an early exploration rather than a committed API. Feedback about the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"design, the use cases, and the trade-offs would be especially valuable as the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"idea develops."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"share-your-ideas","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Share your ideas"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The roadmap will evolve as these experiments produce results. If you have"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"feedback, use cases, or ideas for making "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/core"},{"t":"text","text":" more robust and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"type-safe, please share them through "},{"t":"link","href":"https://github.com/craft-ts/craft-ts/discussions","external":true,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"GitHub Discussions"}]},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"or "},{"t":"link","href":"https://github.com/craft-ts/craft-ts/issues","external":true,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"GitHub Issues"}]},{"t":"text","text":"."}]}],"outline":[{"level":2,"id":"near-term-priorities","text":"Near-term priorities"},{"level":3,"id":"ssr-as-a-craft-host","text":"SSR as a Craft host"},{"level":3,"id":"real-world-integration-and-stability","text":"Real-world integration and stability"},{"level":2,"id":"type-safe-design-systems","text":"Type-safe design systems"},{"level":2,"id":"tooling-for-understanding-changes","text":"Tooling for understanding changes"},{"level":2,"id":"typed-streams-craft-ts-stream","text":"Typed streams (@craft-ts/stream)"},{"level":2,"id":"longer-term-exploration-type-safe-server-functions","text":"Longer-term exploration: type-safe server functions"},{"level":2,"id":"share-your-ideas","text":"Share your ideas"}]}